5 Conclusions
In the paper, we propose a novel cross-domain recognition algorithm termed manifold transfer subspace learning based on double relaxed discriminative regression (MTSLDRDR) for unsupervised domain adaptation. Specifically, both the low-rank and sparsity constraints are firstly utilized to bridge the source and target domain in a projected subspace. Secondly, the two transformation matrices are introduced to better characterize the global structure information of two domains, which can effectively improve the robustness to outliers. Meanwhile, the structure consistency term is introduced for reducing the domain discrepancy of the obtained couple subspaces, which can make two projected matrices capture the resemblance among the samples with the same semantics from different domains. Thirdly, the between-graph and within-graph based

